# modules/print/env.schema — KEY=description:required|optional
#
# Retargeted onto ghcr.io/kisaesdevlab/vibe-printer (see compose.yml). The
# image reads only VIBE_PRINT_*-prefixed variables and ignores everything else,
# so the keys below are what this module needs from the shared .env, not the
# app's full configuration surface.
#
# GONE, and why: POSTGRES_USER / POSTGRES_PASSWORD (the real product is SQLite,
# and the `vibe_print` database is no longer created), SENTINEL_DATA_DIR (no
# wildcard certificate mount — the gateway serves plain HTTP inside the mesh),
# and PRINT_SPOOL_HOLD_HOURS (held release does not exist yet upstream).
VIBE_PRINT_SECRET=Shared bearer secret gating /admin and every /v1 call. The service refuses to boot when empty; generated once by lib/secrets.sh and preserved across re-runs. Rotating it cuts off every caller and every signed-in admin at the same instant:required
MESH_BIND_IP=Mesh interface IP. The gateway's only listener (8632 -> container 8080) binds here and nowhere else:required
TZ=Firm timezone; print audit timestamps render in it:optional
PRINT_JOB_RETENTION_DAYS=Days a completed job row survives before the retention sweep prunes it (default 30):optional
PRINT_AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS=Days the hash-chained print audit log is kept (default 365). Check the firm's own retention policy before shortening:optional
ONSITE_SUBNETS=Comma-separated firm on-premises CIDRs. RESERVED: Decision 26's on-site-direct / off-site-held policy needs the held-release feature, which does not exist upstream yet. Consumed today only by printer-network-policy.sh:optional
PRINTER_SUBNETS=Printer VLAN or NetBird-routed printer CIDRs; consumed by printer-network-policy.sh:optional
PRINTER_IFACE=Host interface facing the printer VLAN, when printers are not NetBird-routed:optional
